    "name": "Hopf Fibers",
    "projectionMode": 1,
    "renderMode": 1,
    "scriptCode": "// --- HOPF FIBERS ---\n// Points of the 3-sphere: (cos(eta)*cos(u), cos(eta)*sin(u), sin(eta)*cos(u + a),\n// sin(eta)*sin(u + a)). For fixed eta and a this is a great circle, a FIBER of\n// the Hopf fibration; any two fibers are linked once. Even meshes lie on the\n// Clifford torus (eta = 45 degrees), odd meshes on a thinner torus; each family\n// is spread evenly by the angle a. The Meshes field sets how many fibers.\n// The curves live in 4D: the 4D rotations show them from new sides.\n//MESH_BEGIN\nu: 0, TAU, 200\nv: 0, TAU, 32\n//MESH_END\nbool clifford = mod(mesh, 2.0) < 0.5;\nfloat eta = clifford ? 0.78539816 : 0.42;\nfloat n = clifford ? ceil(meshes * 0.5) : max(floor(meshes * 0.5), 1.0);\nfloat a = floor(mesh * 0.5) * 6.28318531 / n;\nreturn vec4(cos(eta)*cos(u), cos(eta)*sin(u), sin(eta)*cos(u + a), sin(eta)*sin(u + a));\n",
    "steps": 120,
